WEBVTT

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:10.700
This is Gommage, a replay and observability layer
for AI agents that operate inside Jira workflows

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.000
The problem we're solving is simple
Agents don't just answer questions anymore

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.200
They write tickets and emails, change statuses,
investigate incidents, and close work

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.750
When something goes wrong, the failure often
looks like success. The ticket is marked as done,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:29.250
the workflow is completed, and no exception
is thrown. But the customer never got helped

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.100
This is the class of failure
Gommage is designed to catch

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.100
So we're introducing Gommage

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.500
Gommage records an agent execution record
for every run

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.800
Underneath, we wrap the agent's LLM calls
and tool calls

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:52.000
Every step gets captured, the model prompt,
the model decision,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.720
the tool name, the parameter, the tool result,
the timing, the context, and whether the tool was side-effecting.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.400
Instead of asking why the ticket is done, we can ask
what exactly the agent saw, decided, and executed

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:14.800
Here, step five is email.send
We can see that the “to” parameter is empty

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:25.750
For step six, it's going to close the ticket
even though the workflow has operationally failed

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:32.400
The agent didn't crash
It silently did the wrong thing

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.500
We select replay in debug mode,
and we can see the replicated run

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.800
The important thing is that replay is safe
Side-effecting tools are blocked or mocked

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:56.700
We can replay the agent without sending emails,
modifying Jira, posting to Slack, or making the incident worse

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:03.200
It's here, the notification tool
was called with no recipient

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:11.610
I'm going to change this,
and we can see the updated result

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:25.370
We continue execution from this point
The customer response would be present in production
